# YTLive transport watchdog - the root-only rungs of its recovery ladder, and NOTHING else.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (tracker row T-38). bin/net_watch.sh runs as a launchd USER agent, so it has
# no root: it cannot renew a DHCP lease with `ipconfig`, and it cannot flush the resolver cache.
# Without this rule the ladder stops at the no-sudo `networksetup` actions, and a wedged lease
# therefore needs a human - which is exactly the failure this project keeps paying for.
#
# SCOPE. Three exact commands, for one user, with no shell, no wildcards and no ALL. A wildcard
# in an argument is how "renew DHCP on en0" quietly becomes something else, and the point of the
# rule is that the watchdog can do these three things and nothing more. `killall -HUP
# mDNSResponder` is deliberately NOT here: it is a heavier alternative to `dscacheutil` that no
# code path calls, and an unused grant is still a grant. If a fifth becomes necessary, add it
# deliberately and say why in this comment.
#
# INSTALLED AND VERIFIED BY bin/harden-host.sh, which substitutes __YT_USER__, proves the result
# with `visudo -cf` BEFORE it can land in /etc/sudoers.d/, and installs it 0440 root:wheel:
#
#     sudo bin/harden-host.sh --go      # install (also does the pmset hardening)
#     bin/harden-host.sh --check        # verify
#
# A malformed file in /etc/sudoers.d/ can make sudo refuse EVERYTHING, including the rule that
# lets you fix it - which is why nothing here is ever written without a parse check first.
__YT_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/ipconfig set en0 DHCP
__YT_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/sbin/ipconfig set en2 DHCP
__YT_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/dscacheutil -flushcache
